{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011Cfbeb1bEMBF9VotVfgbns","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The build phase is done: `@one-a-day/sports/swim-time-drop-card/v1` is built, three variants are rendered, and variant c is the one left in `src/`.\n\n## What was built\n\nA still card for one swimmer at one meet: per event the entry time, the time swum, the drop in seconds, a bar and the standard chip. The defaults show an invented swimmer with six swims and give `5 of 6 swims faster` / `14.82 s dropped`.\n\n| Variant | The one idea | Gate | Render | What the stills show |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| a | bar = share of the entry time dropped | clean | ok | Fair between a 50 and a 200, but `-0.87` sits over a longer bar than `-4.01` and only the footnote explains why |\n| b | bar = seconds dropped | clean | ok | Bar and printed number agree, but the 50s shrink to stubs |\n| c | a, with each bar's percent printed at its end | clean | ok | Every bar carries its own number; clearest in landscape and portrait |\n\nI left **c** in place because it fixes the two-unit confusion the brief flagged as the risk in a.\n\n## Checks\n\n- **Build gate:** `npm run build` is clean for this template. The two warnings it prints belong to older frozen templates.\n- **Tests:** the template's 33 tests pass on the final source. The last full `npm test` (261 jest tests, 56 pipeline tests) passed before two small final layout tweaks and was not rerun after them.\n- **Renders:** all three variants exit 0 at landscape, portrait and square, with no degraded render and a six-page tutorial each.\n- **Tutorial pages:** I viewed variant a's problem, solution and usage pages and nothing clips. The problem page quotes the recaps with children's names replaced by `[swimmer]`. Variant c's regenerated pages (one solution sentence and one usage line changed) rendered cleanly but I did not view them.\n\n## Weak spots, recorded in `30-build.md`\n\n- Variant c's bar labels are the smallest data on the square card: 23 px with six rows, 16 px with eight.\n- A card with one or two swims leaves the middle of the square empty, as the brief asked rather than slab rows.\n- A 21-character event name (`400 Individual Medley`) drops the event column to 24 px in an eight-row square.\n- Copy that cannot fit at the size floor is refused with an error naming the field and canvas. This only triggers far below the smallest contract canvas.\n- The template does not read `.hy3`/`.cl2` files; the caller parses the results and supplies the rows and the standards.\n\nTwo things differ from the brief or scaffold:\n\n- I dropped \"best times\" from the scaffold's `who` line, which was one character over the 160 limit.\n- With long copy on square or portrait, the meet and details each take their own line instead of sharing one.\n\n`state.json` now has `scaffolded: true`, `variants: [\"a\",\"b\",\"c\"]`, `inPlace: \"c\"`, `build: \"done\"`. Nothing was committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1143,"cache_read_input_tokens":289674,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1143},"output_tokens":728,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69fab120-65e8-492e-b76a-c27ffd29396a","uuid":"72e2c1e9-a7a4-4873-987d-3953cfbfe060","timestamp":"2026-10-01T14:08:40.340Z","request_id":"req_011Cfbeaz7Bsa1xZTjyt5nBA"}
